Date Completed: 6-15-26)","date":null,"url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billanalysis/Senate/htm/2026-SFA-1026-G.htm","type":"HTML"}],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would change the rules for how members of a domestic credit union can amend its bylaws or charter, which is the basic set of rules for the credit union. It would let members approve those changes, give or take back power from the credit union board to make them, and require notice of any such proposal before the meeting. Changes would still need review and approval by the director, except for bylaw changes that are only logistical.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MI-2025-HB6430":{"id":"MI-2025-HB6430","passed":false,"number":"HB 6430","title":"Occupations: individual licensing and registration; issuance of initial or renewal license or registration; modify for certain occupations. Amends sec. 411 of 1980 PA 299 (MCL 339.411).","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-10-14","sponsor":{"name":"Bill Schuette","party":"R","state":"MI","district":"95"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-21","text":"bill electronically reproduced 10/14/2026","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"introduced by Representative Rep. Bill Schuette","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"read a first time","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"referred to Committee on Regulatory Reform","chamber":"House"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Occupations: individual licensing and registration, State agencies (existing): licensing and regulatory affairs","url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/Bills/Bill?ObjectName=2026-HB-6430","textUrl":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6430.htm","versions":[{"label":"House Introduced Bill","date":null,"url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/House/htm/2026-HIB-6430.htm","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would change the rules for getting or renewing many Michigan occupational licenses and registrations. It would set a 90-day deadline for the department to issue an initial or renewal license after a complete application is filed, with shorter 30-day timing for real estate brokers and associate brokers, and it would require refunds or a 15% fee cut if the deadline is missed. It would also spell out late renewal, reinstatement, and military-duty exemption rules for licensed workers and registrants, and it would affect many occupations listed in the bill.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MI-2025-SB1209":{"id":"MI-2025-SB1209","passed":false,"number":"SB 1209","title":"Military affairs: other; release of the Michigan National Guard into active duty combat without an official act of Congress; prohibit. Amends 1967 PA 150 (MCL 32.501 - 32.851) by adding sec. 203.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-10-14","sponsor":{"name":"Jonathan Lindsey","party":"R","state":"MI","district":"17"},"cosponsors":[{"name":"Edward W. McBroom","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Mary Cavanagh","party":"D","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Jim Runestad","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Jeff Irwin","party":"D","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Joseph N. Bellino Jr.","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":5,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"INTRODUCED BY SENATOR JONATHAN LINDSEY","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"REFERRED TO COMMITTEE ON VETERANS AND EMERGENCY SERVICES","chamber":"Senate"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Military affairs: other, State agencies (existing): military and veterans affairs","url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/Bills/Bill?ObjectName=2026-SB-1209","textUrl":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/Senate/htm/2026-SIB-1209.htm","versions":[{"label":"Senate Introduced Bill","date":null,"url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/Senate/htm/2026-SIB-1209.htm","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would bar the Michigan National Guard from being sent into active duty combat unless Congress has declared war or taken another official action to call up the state militia. It would apply only if 25 or more states pass a similar law. The governor would have to take the steps needed to follow this rule.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MI-2025-SB1202":{"id":"MI-2025-SB1202","passed":false,"number":"SB 1202","title":"Appropriations: supplemental; funding for the animal agriculture alliance; provide for. Creates appropriation act.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-10-14","sponsor":{"name":"Roger Victory","party":"R","state":"MI","district":"31"},"cosponsors":[{"name":"Kevin Daley","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Rick Outman","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Edward W. McBroom","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Joseph N. Bellino Jr.","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Dan Lauwers","party":"R","state":"MI","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":5,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"INTRODUCED BY SENATOR ROGER VICTORY","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-10-14","text":"REFERRED TO COMMITTEE ON APPROPRIATIONS","chamber":"Senate"}],"law":null,"policyArea":"Appropriations: supplemental","url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/Bills/Bill?ObjectName=2026-SB-1202","textUrl":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/Senate/htm/2026-SIB-1202.htm","versions":[{"label":"Senate Introduced Bill","date":null,"url":"https://legislature.mi.gov/documents/2025-2026/billintroduced/Senate/htm/2026-SIB-1202.htm","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would change state spending for fiscal year 2026-27 and give $2.5 million to the Michigan animal agriculture alliance through the agriculture department. It also cuts $1.5 million from the labor and economic opportunity department and $1 million from the natural resources department. The text says the new spending rules would apply to these appropriations and that some prior spending authority would end.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"MI-2025-SB791":{"id":"MI-2025-SB791","passed":false,"number":"SB 791","title":"Highways: memorial; portion of I-475; designate as the \"St. John Street Community Memorial Highway\". Amends 2001 PA 142 (MCL 250.1001 - 250.2092) by adding sec. 124.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-02-19","sponsor":{"name":"John Cherry","party":"D","state":"MI","district":"27"},"cosponsors":[],"cosponsorCount":0,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"received on 10/01/2026","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"read a first time","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-06","text":"referred to Committee on Transportation and Infrastructure","chamber":"House"},{"date":"2026-10-01","text":"PASSED ROLL CALL # 258 YEAS 33 NAYS 3 EXCUSED 2 NOT VOTING 0","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-09-10","text":"REPORTED BY COMMITTEE OF THE WHOLE FAVORABLY WITHOUT AMENDMENT(S)","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-09-10","text":"PLACED ON ORDER OF THIRD READING","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-06-25","text":"REPORTED FAVORABLY WITHOUT AMENDMENT 6/24/2026","chamber":"Senate"},{"date":"2026-06-25","text":"REFERRED TO COMMITTEE OF THE WHOLE","chamber":"Se